abstract: "A parallel kernel-independent FMM library for particle and volume potentials. It solves Stokes, Poisson and Helmholtz problems on the unit cube, with free-space or periodic boundary conditions, by a volume potential integral equation formulation accelerated by the kernel-independent fast multipole method."
repository-code: "https://github.com/dmalhotra/pvfmm"
url: "https://pvfmm.readthedocs.io"
license: LGPL-3.0-only
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
